1
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:44,200
‎-Good morning.
‎-Good morning.

3
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,560
‎-Good morning.
‎-Good morning.

4
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:47,480
‎-Okay.
‎-Good.

5
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:50,160
Morning.

6
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:51,640
You keep pushing this hard.

7
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:52,880
Not afraid of a heart attack?

8
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,360
Right back at you.

9
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:58,160
Weren't you sending files
in the group chat until 2 a.m.?

10
00:01:58,240 --> 00:01:59,160
Coffee?

11
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:00,520
Sure.

12
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:03,720
I can't compete with you.

13
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:06,760
You're the only newbie
who's landed a project on your own.

14
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:09,919
It's just project initiation follow-up,

15
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:12,440
writing technical specs and proposals.

16
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:15,000
Once the contract is signed,
a project manager will take over.

17
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:17,120
We grunts just get to do the scut work.

18
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:19,640
What else?

19
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,080
You want to take over the whole project?

20
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:27,040
I just got the Bolo Culture project.

21
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:29,000
Quit being snarky
first thing in the morning.

22
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:30,920
Aren't you aiming to be a partner?

23
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,160
Why take an interest
in my small-scale project?

24
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:34,600
I'm heading down.

25
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:36,160
Of course I don't care.

26
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:38,760
But don't act weak.

27
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:40,320
Doesn't fit your image.

28
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:43,920
Bring out that killer instinct you used
to poach Lin Long's project.

29
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,840
I like it.

30
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,040
You two…?

31
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:54,960
Go on.

32
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,040
I'm grabbing breakfast downstairs.
Need anything?

33
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:01,160
-She likes the chicken breast panini.
-Got it.

34
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:02,760
Thanks.

35
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:07,560
What do you get
out of spilling my private business?

36
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,880
At least it makes people think
we're friends.

37
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:13,280
Keeps the Deng Anran types off my back.

38
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:14,840
Work itself is exhausting enough.

39
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:18,120
I don't have the energy
for office drama dumber

40
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,280
than a soap opera.

41
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:20,800
Smart.

42
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,520
But let's get one thing straight.

43
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,840
I'm keeping you as my right hand,

44
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:27,680
not my friend.

45
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:31,880
Okay by me. Right hand means trust.

46
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:45,120
Actually, I've always wondered.

47
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:48,680
We only met when we joined the company,
so why have you always been

48
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:50,560
so nice to me?

49
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:51,880
Because I like you.

50
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,440
You really don't remember?

51
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,080
Remember what?

52
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:08,280
Back in the day, by Daming Lake,

53
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,320
you were Xia Yuhe.

54
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:13,880
Oh my God. You actually tell jokes.

55
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:22,760
Are you okay?

56
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:32,600
Hello?

57
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:33,920
Did you zone out?

58
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:37,920
No.

59
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:40,560
I was just thinking

60
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:43,240
about how many newbies

61
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:45,040
will actually show up
for the weekend outdoor challenge.

62
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,120
How many?

63
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,320
All that overtime fried your brain?

64
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:52,080
Didn't you see both newbie teams are gone?

65
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:56,520
The three-month mark is the first hurdle.

66
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:03,200
New colleagues,

67
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:05,840
the rules for this new hire challenge
are straightforward.

68
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:08,480
Use your strategy and your courage.

69
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:11,160
First team to reach the finish line wins.

70
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:13,920
The winning team

71
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:18,560
gets a two-week training
at the North America HQ at year-end.

72
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:20,440
Great!

73
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:22,080
You each have a hand-drawn map.

74
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,400
Mountain route, water route,
and forest route.

75
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:25,040
Each team can choose their own path.

76
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:27,200
The goal is to reach
the destination fast and efficiently.

77
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:30,160
Each team has a professional
outdoor guide for safety.

78
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:32,480
Lu Le and I will supervise
to ensure fairness.

79
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:34,040
Other than that, you're on your own.

80
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,760
-Move!
-Good luck.

81
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:36,760
-Go!
-Go!

82
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:37,840
MAXMISE CONSULTING STORM CHALLENGE CAMP

83
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:43,720
Want to race?

84
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:46,200
If you lose, we switch places.

85
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:48,600
I'll be the partner,
and you're the right hand.

86
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:52,720
You know, your name is pretty good.

87
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:53,960
"Chi" means being late. Great omen!

88
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,560
See you at the finish line.

89
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,080
-Off we go!
-Let's go.

90
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:01,680
Sorry.

91
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:03,520
Tianna!

92
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:04,480
Hurry!

93
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:20,920
Thanks.

94
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,600
This trekking pole is non-slip. Take it.

95
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:25,360
I'm fine. I just didn't see
the path clearly.

96
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:26,280
Aren't you trying to win?

97
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:28,200
If you slip and get hurt, you can't win.

98
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:30,320
I'm not on the team. I don't have to walk.

99
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:33,640
Okay.

100
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,840
I'll return it in a bit.

101
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:36,720
No need to be so formal with me.

102
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:51,120
You're not going to hold
the whole team back, are you?

103
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,080
No need.

104
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,880
I know first aid. I'll do it myself.

105
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:13,600
Come on.

106
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,480
You know first aid for helping others.

107
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:19,160
Not so easy when it's yourself, is it?

108
00:07:20,320 --> 00:07:21,160
Here.

109
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:29,400
Seriously, why are you so guarded?

110
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:33,480
You really think everyone
is after your dad's money?

111
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:37,200
Red team!

112
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:38,120
-Coming.
-Coming.

113
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,440
Let's talk it over.

114
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:40,360
I just checked the map.

115
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:42,280
Why don't we take the mountain route?

116
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,360
The water route is shorter,

117
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:45,320
but the current's too strong.
It's kind of dangerous.

118
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:48,680
There's a bridge up ahead
that leads to the mountain path.

119
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:50,160
It adds about three kilometers.

120
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:51,480
But I think we might
actually be faster that way.

121
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,920
What do you all think?

122
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,120
-Sure. It's fine with me.
-Sounds good.

123
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:01,720
The red team excels at analyzing materials
and has strong command over projects.

124
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:03,200
I took a look.

125
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:05,960
Everyone on the team has to reach
the finish line together to win,

126
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:08,000
but my foot's injured. I can't go far.

127
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:10,520
The water route is tough,
but it's the shortest.

128
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:11,600
Everyone, get your ropes out.

129
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:12,720
-Okay.
-Okay.

130
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,960
The blue team has strong leadership

131
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,080
and is good at handling pressure
and working together.

132
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:20,200
The yellow team has great team spirit.

133
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:22,760
I've posted everyone's scores
in the group chat.

134
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:23,680
Check them out.

135
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:26,320
The blue team's taking
the shortcut across the stream.

136
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:27,760
<i>Tell them to stay safe.</i>

137
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:31,040
Don't worry. The guide said
Bu Tianna looks professionally trained.

138
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:32,080
It should be fine.

139
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:34,799
They've all secured their safety ropes,
bu Tianna's bringing up the rear.

140
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:37,000
Most of the team
has already crossed safely.

141
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:24,920
-Keep going!
-Go!

142
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,080
-You got this!
-Here, drink some water.

143
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:28,400
Almost there! Come on!

144
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:30,440
-Nice work.
-Keep going!

145
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:31,520
-Almost there!
-Where are they?

146
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:32,480
-Zhao Heng. Tianna.
-Keep going!

147
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:33,920
-Come on!
-Come on!

148
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,920
-Keep going!
-Almost there!

149
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:38,960
Su Su, come on!

150
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:40,480
-Su Su, go!
-Go!

151
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:43,040
-Su Su, come on!
-Su Su, come on!

152
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:44,320
-Go for it!
-Go for it!

153
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:45,520
Zhao Heng, Tianna, come on!

154
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,440
Su Su!

155
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:48,600
‎-Come on!
‎-Go!

156
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:50,640
‎-Come on!
‎-Go!

157
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:52,800
Su Su, come on! Su Su, you've got this!

158
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:53,760
-Go!
-Go!

159
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:57,960
‎You got this!

160
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:00,680
Come on.

161
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,160
Get on my back. Hop on.

162
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:04,680
This isn't for you.
It's for the whole team.

163
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,320
Come on!

164
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:10,960
Go!

165
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:12,880
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

166
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:15,080
-Su Su, come on!
-Su Su, come on!

167
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:16,320
-You got this!
-You got this!

168
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:21,760
Almost there!

169
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,360
-Go, go!
-Go, go!

170
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:25,280
-Go for it!
-Go for it!

171
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,880
MAXMISE CONSULTING STORM CHALLENGE CAMP
FINISH LINE

172
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:32,920
Nice.

173
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:35,120
Are you okay? You did great.

174
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:36,760
Well done.

175
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,680
Congratulations to our champions,
blue team!

176
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,920
This event is officially a success.

177
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,800
Thanks to everyone for giving it your all!

178
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:02,520
Did you make this?

179
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:06,120
This looks like a commercial. Nice work.

180
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,960
It's not that I did anything amazing.

181
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:10,000
It's just that everyone's emotions
were so real.

182
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:14,080
They call it building team spirit,

183
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:15,960
trust, and courage.

184
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:16,880
But really,

185
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:19,560
they just want us to get high
on that sense of satisfaction

186
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:21,000
from overcoming challenges.

187
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,920
And you know what? We totally fall for it.

188
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:54,640
Hey,

189
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,920
I took some photos of you back there.

190
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,400
Let me add you on WeChat
and send them over.

191
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:04,440
ZHAO HENG, ADD TO CONTACTS

192
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:12,960
ADD IMAGE TO REMARK

193
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,160
Nice shots.

194
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:29,360
Free for lunch? My treat.

195
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:40,720
So good!

196
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:43,960
Fancy restaurants really are different.

197
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:45,600
Great atmosphere. Great food.

198
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:47,840
How did you know I love lamb chops?

199
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:49,920
It's perfect for me!

200
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:53,200
When I was a kid, I herded sheep
on those Northwestern hillsides.

201
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,920
Blue skies. Green grass.

202
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,440
Very pastoral.

203
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:59,760
But even the best view
can't fill your stomach.

204
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:02,800
Back then, my family didn't have much.

205
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:04,360
All I had for lunch every day
was a dry mantou.

206
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:05,560
No way that was enough.

207
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:10,000
So from then on,
I'd stare at those little bleating sheep

208
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:13,800
and swear that once I got to college,
I'd eat all the lamb I wanted.

209
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:16,160
Well? Pretty good story?

210
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:18,840
Pretty good.

211
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:21,280
But the better part is still coming.

212
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:22,720
Let me borrow your phone.

213
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:23,640
Unlock it.

214
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:36,200
‎CHOOSE PICTURES

215
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:38,720
DELETED

216
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:42,920
Last time I borrowed
your ice pack and bandages

217
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,640
and you carried me.

218
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:47,000
So today I bought you lunch
and kept you company.

219
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:49,240
Materially and emotionally, we're even.

220
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:51,880
And I already deleted those photos of me
on your phone.

221
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:52,960
Stop sneaking photos of me from now on.

222
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:54,480
If you do it again,

223
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:56,640
I'll report you to the company
for harassment.

224
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:57,600
Bye.

225
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:00,280
I've sent you the 3,000
for the lunch bill.

226
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,440
Wait, I wasn't sneaking photos of you.
I wasn't!

227
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:04,240
Sir! Sir, you haven't paid yet.

228
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:05,160
Come on.

229
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:11,040
Is paying really that important?

230
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:15,640
I wasn't taking sneaky photos.

231
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:17,280
They were just event photos.

232
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:18,880
Besides, we're colleagues.

233
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:20,680
Why make it so awkward?

234
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:23,720
-We're just colleagues.
-Exactly.

235
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:25,840
Don't be so tense. Relax.

236
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:27,320
It's such a nice afternoon.

237
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:29,040
Let's talk about something fun--

238
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:31,280
Is there anything fun
to talk about with you?

239
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:33,280
Every word you say is calculated.

240
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,480
I've met plenty of people like you.

241
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,040
Stop following me.

242
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,080
What are you doing?

243
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:43,160
When I was hurt,

244
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:45,960
you started with that blunt confession
to throw me off.

245
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:47,440
Your last name is Bu.

246
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:50,960
Marrying you would save me
50 years of work.

247
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:53,640
Anyway, I don't have
much to do outside work.

248
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:54,640
So why don't I give it a shot?

249
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:56,560
You helped me and praised me

250
00:14:56,640 --> 00:14:59,440
just to create contrast
and leave an impression.

251
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:01,840
You really think everyone
is after your dad's money?

252
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:04,960
You're pretty and capable.

253
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:06,400
Can't I just be drawn to your personality?

254
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:08,520
Then you laid out your sob story,

255
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:12,280
making your past
sound romantic and pitiful.

256
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:14,520
Any soft-hearted girl
would've fallen for it.

257
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:16,680
You turned Hejun Management's
six client-attraction tactics

258
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:18,080
into a pick-up routine.

259
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:19,400
Not bad at all.

260
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,080
You saw right through me.

261
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:25,560
This is embarrassing.

262
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:27,160
Don't sell yourself short.

263
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:31,040
These moves are more than enough
for a simple, love-first girl.

264
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:35,640
Too bad I know exactly
the plays and agenda

265
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:37,320
of scheming guys like you.

266
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:39,640
You've been hurt before?

267
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:43,880
-None of your business.
-The trick doesn't have to be new.

268
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:45,240
What matters is,

269
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:47,360
did it work on you?

270
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:55,960
I came to Maxmise to be a partner,
not to date.

271
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:59,320
You're already thinking about dating?

272
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:04,240
Wait.

273
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:12,520
Stop.

274
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,360
Stop laughing.

275
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:41,520
You're like a bobblehead.

276
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:50,280
He used all six of Hejun's tactics on me.

277
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:51,320
He's something else.

278
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:55,360
Su Su?

279
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:00,240
Sha Sha told me

280
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:03,960
my client interface
hasn't been proactive enough.

281
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:07,480
My performance under pressure at
the challenge camp was also just average.

282
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:09,839
She suggested I transfer
to the visualization team.

283
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:16,880
The visualization team?

284
00:17:19,119 --> 00:17:22,200
It's the team
that just does PowerPoint slides.

285
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:24,079
Sounds fancy,

286
00:17:24,599 --> 00:17:27,839
but it's basically
a demotion to back-office support.

287
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,160
You can never come back to consulting.

288
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:32,280
Isn't the challenge camp
just a team-building thing?

289
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:34,560
They actually use it
as an evaluation tool?

290
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:36,400
And what does
"average under pressure" even mean?

291
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:38,720
Su Su was sprinting while crying.

292
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:41,200
You didn't know that?

293
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:44,160
Using the challenge camp
as a simulated test for the staff

294
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:45,920
has always been a Maxmise tradition.

295
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:49,320
The problem might be that she cried.

296
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:52,600
In consulting, the last thing you want
is to be emotional.

297
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,800
It is what it is. Reality's harsh.

298
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:55,960
It all comes down to ability.

299
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:04,000
Oh, keep a close eye
on the Bolo Culture project.

300
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:06,160
You only get credit
once the contract is actually signed.

301
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:08,960
Do you think she'll quit?

302
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:11,200
I'm guessing she will.

303
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:13,320
Support departments
are way behind business units

304
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:15,160
in both status and pay.

305
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:19,440
Within a week,
someone new will take her place.

306
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,440
Not bad.

307
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:37,520
I approve of this proposal.

308
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,600
So when can we sign?

309
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:43,040
Send me the contract first.
I'll have Legal review it.

310
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:44,040
Okay.

311
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:45,400
By the way,

312
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:48,920
Maxmise isn't going
to let a young girl like you handle

313
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,200
a project this big alone, are they?

314
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:51,800
Of course not.

315
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:54,200
We'll set up a project team
right after signing.

316
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:56,440
With a project manager leading it,

317
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:59,320
plus partners, consultants,
data folks, and analysts like me.

318
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:04,480
You're playing me.

319
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,040
Payment is due after signing.

320
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:07,960
So far,

321
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:10,480
you've only come to our office
for a few interviews

322
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:11,600
and written some papers.

323
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:13,600
All using your public templates.

324
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:16,600
You don't even know
what Qingyi Literature looks like

325
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:18,240
or how many IPs they have.

326
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:22,360
When our board asks me
about the project's viability,

327
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:23,560
what do I say?

328
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:26,600
I've read a lot of Qingyi's iconic works,

329
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:28,000
and I have all the IP library materials.

330
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:29,120
But you're right.

331
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:32,120
I'd love to join you
for a site visit if that works for you.

332
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:33,240
Perfect.

333
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:35,720
I'm heading to their HQ tomorrow anyway.

334
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:36,800
See you early tomorrow.

335
00:19:39,040 --> 00:19:40,280
Early tomorrow?

336
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:42,160
Yeah. Flight leaves at 7 a.m.

337
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:43,920
You have two hours to get ready.

338
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:48,880
<i>Hey, Zhao Heng.</i>

339
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:50,760
Got a sec to talk?

340
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,240
Did you see my WeChat message?

341
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:54,360
I have to take
a last-minute business trip.

342
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:57,360
I already applied through the system,

343
00:19:57,440 --> 00:19:58,720
and Ms. Lin approved it.

344
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:01,480
Can you find the company
travel reimbursement policy for me?

345
00:20:01,560 --> 00:20:03,840
I couldn't locate that file. Sure.

346
00:20:04,440 --> 00:20:05,960
Thanks. I know.

347
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:09,720
NO VEHICLES AVAILABLE NEARBY

348
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:10,600
YOUR ORDER HAS TIMED OUT
PLEASE REQUEST A NEW RIDE

349
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:49,440
Xu Chi!

350
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,120
What's going on?

351
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:58,000
Well, can you drop me
at the subway station?

352
00:20:58,080 --> 00:20:59,240
I need to get to the airport.

353
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:00,880
-Get in.
-Great.

354
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:07,440
Aren't you here on a business trip?

355
00:21:07,520 --> 00:21:09,400
Why are you driving yourself
to the airport?

356
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:11,760
Who said I'm on a business trip?

357
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:14,560
-Thank you.
-I'm based here from now on.

358
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:17,480
I'm going to Hong Kong, China.
Back tomorrow afternoon.

359
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,680
Parking at the airport is convenient.

360
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:21,360
Saves me from having
an unreliable assistant

361
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:22,560
pick me up wrong again.

362
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:32,680
Where are you going?

363
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:34,600
Guangzhou.

364
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:36,200
I am doing research with a client.

365
00:21:36,280 --> 00:21:37,520
With your mentor?

366
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:39,960
She told me to go alone.

367
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:42,880
Didn't Maxmise assign you a new mentor?

368
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:46,360
You can't become a consultant
by figuring it all out on your own.

369
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:48,800
This isn't a task for a newbie.

370
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:50,600
I know.

371
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,320
But I still want to try.

372
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:57,120
By the way, I saw your suitcase earlier.

373
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:58,040
It's cute.

374
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:00,320
Really?

375
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:01,480
I bought it in college.

376
00:22:01,560 --> 00:22:04,040
Let me give you some advice.
Consultants should stick

377
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:06,400
to a few well-known business brands
for their suitcases.

378
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:08,920
For women, go with a lightweight
zippered fabric suitcase.

379
00:22:09,560 --> 00:22:11,280
It holds more and doesn't look bad
if it gets scuffed.

380
00:22:11,360 --> 00:22:14,120
Stick to black, navy blue, or light brown.

381
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:16,520
No bright colors. No cartoon stickers.

382
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:18,000
Nothing over 20 inches.

383
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:19,760
It must be carry-on size.

384
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:21,320
It saves you from lost luggage

385
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:24,600
and saves half an hour at check-in.

386
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:28,720
A consultant charges clients 25,000 a day.

387
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:29,640
Over ten hours,

388
00:22:29,720 --> 00:22:32,600
one trip saves you 2,500.

389
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:36,680
But a carry-on is too small.

390
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:37,960
What if the trip's over three days?

391
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:40,680
Standard consultant setup
is a canvas duffel

392
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:41,800
on top of the suitcase,

393
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:44,520
plus a backpack for your laptop.

394
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:46,680
If you have time,
go swap it out at the airport.

395
00:22:58,160 --> 00:22:59,520
Let me get it.

396
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:08,040
Thank you so much.

397
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:10,480
Let's add each other on WeChat.

398
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:12,600
Your mentor's ignoring you anyway.

399
00:23:13,120 --> 00:23:15,760
If you have questions,
I can be your off-site coach.

400
00:23:15,840 --> 00:23:16,720
Sure.

401
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:20,440
Let me scan yours.

402
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:27,520
YE THE LEGEND

403
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:30,400
Ye the Legend?

404
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:33,520
You give people nicknames
this over-the-top now?

405
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:37,600
It's not over-the-top.

406
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,080
You're my idol.

407
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:41,240
Oh nice, now you're laying it on thick.

408
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:43,360
I'm not. I mean it.

409
00:23:45,640 --> 00:23:46,760
I…

410
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:51,600
I've been trying hard to become
a qualified consultant as soon as I can.

411
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:54,640
Not just for the money
and my mom's old apartment.

412
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:57,960
I also hope that one day,

413
00:23:58,040 --> 00:24:01,440
I can be as strong and smart as you,

414
00:24:01,520 --> 00:24:04,160
stay calm, and handle anything with ease.

415
00:24:05,720 --> 00:24:06,920
With all that praise,

416
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:08,720
you'll definitely make it.

417
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:10,920
And this is your first business trip.

418
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:12,880
So, don't expect
to wow the client right away.

419
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:14,200
Lower your expectations.

420
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:17,200
Try to understand their real situation
and what they truly need.

421
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:19,840
I'm in a hurry to board. Bye.

422
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:37,200
QINGYI LITERATURE

423
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:38,240
That's not how you go about this!

424
00:24:38,320 --> 00:24:39,560
I don't agree with this plan. No way.

425
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:40,480
We haven't even spoken yet,

426
00:24:40,560 --> 00:24:42,120
-and you're already jumping in?
-All these rules and regulations…

427
00:24:42,200 --> 00:24:44,200
Just because you spoke first
doesn't mean you're right. Right?

428
00:24:44,280 --> 00:24:46,280
I'm telling you,
either you make it work, or forget it!

429
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:47,440
I don't have much time!

430
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:48,960
Whatever happens…

431
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:51,720
-I don't care anymore.
-Look what time it is!

432
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:53,200
I'm going to miss my flight. That's it!

433
00:24:53,280 --> 00:24:54,360
Alright. Everyone, sit down!

434
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,080
Are you done yet?

435
00:24:58,680 --> 00:25:00,680
This is a business negotiation,
not a wet market.

436
00:25:04,400 --> 00:25:05,560
I have two more meetings this afternoon.

437
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:06,920
I don't have time to do financial reports.

438
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:09,960
-No, no. I don't have time.
-Just let me see your previous ones.

439
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:14,600
Mr. Li. Liu from our department
will go to your office later

440
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:15,520
to coordinate on the project.

441
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:16,720
QINGYI LITERATURE

442
00:25:20,720 --> 00:25:22,280
So, what did you learn from this trip?

443
00:25:24,320 --> 00:25:26,560
I just went to see
their senior management.

444
00:25:26,640 --> 00:25:28,280
They're not very willing to talk to me.

445
00:25:31,240 --> 00:25:33,080
I paid real money to acquire the company,

446
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:35,400
and they're still
paying lip service to me.

447
00:25:36,080 --> 00:25:38,040
You're a rookie who just showed up.

448
00:25:38,120 --> 00:25:40,560
And you asked their CFO
for payroll reports.

449
00:25:40,640 --> 00:25:41,840
You think they'd give them to you?

450
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:47,680
In my earlier proposal,

451
00:25:47,760 --> 00:25:51,160
I focused heavily on the senior executive
compensation reform plan

452
00:25:51,240 --> 00:25:52,800
for Qingyi Literature.

453
00:25:52,880 --> 00:25:55,520
It emphasizes consistency,
alignment, and granularity.

454
00:25:55,600 --> 00:25:57,440
-Once the project manager takes over--
-Hold on.

455
00:25:59,080 --> 00:26:02,040
Why are you talking like Lin Long
with all that meaningless jargon?

456
00:26:02,120 --> 00:26:04,000
Are you trying to dazzle me
with buzzwords?

457
00:26:04,080 --> 00:26:07,440
I'm telling you, that's what I saw
internet investors do years ago.

458
00:26:08,880 --> 00:26:11,440
No. Bolo is a major internet company,

459
00:26:11,520 --> 00:26:13,480
so I wanted to use some industry terms.

460
00:26:13,560 --> 00:26:14,600
Enough. Stop explaining.

461
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:17,000
I'm paying you consultants big money

462
00:26:17,080 --> 00:26:19,520
to help Qingyi Literature
integrate into us smoothly.

463
00:26:20,200 --> 00:26:22,480
Yes, your arrangements
for regular employees are not bad.

464
00:26:22,560 --> 00:26:25,960
But what I want
is a more effective overall solution,

465
00:26:26,040 --> 00:26:28,720
not some simple compensation reform deck.

466
00:26:32,960 --> 00:26:33,840
Hello?

467
00:26:35,120 --> 00:26:36,200
Hold on.

468
00:26:36,280 --> 00:26:37,560
Alright. Let's leave it here for now.

469
00:26:37,640 --> 00:26:39,160
We'll catch up in Beijing
when we have time.

470
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:44,320
Go ahead.

471
00:26:50,040 --> 00:26:51,200
They have a lot of demands.

472
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:53,840
Maxmise isn't helping much either.

473
00:26:54,880 --> 00:26:56,920
This acquisition is going to be tough.

474
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:07,680
<i>Your baby is fine,</i>

475
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:10,480
<i>but you really need to rest and relax.</i>

476
00:27:10,560 --> 00:27:14,640
<i>Your spasmodic abdominal pain is</i>
<i>closely linked to your emotional stress.</i>

477
00:27:15,760 --> 00:27:16,680
Rest?

478
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:20,080
Just wait a little longer.

479
00:27:24,720 --> 00:27:26,960
<i>Ms. Lin, are you busy?</i>

480
00:27:27,040 --> 00:27:29,080
<i>Could you get back to me when you can?</i>
<i>It's something urgent!</i>

481
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:30,600
<i>Please get back to me</i>
<i>as soon as you see this.</i>

482
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:37,800
LIN LONG

483
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:57,080
MS. SHA SHA AT MAXMISE

484
00:28:00,280 --> 00:28:01,280
VOICE CALL

485
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:08,160
Hello, Ms. Sha. This is Xu Chi.

486
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:10,360
Sha Sha is on a video call
with US headquarters.

487
00:28:10,440 --> 00:28:12,440
She asked me to take her call. What's up?

488
00:28:17,120 --> 00:28:19,280
It's about the Bolo Culture project.

489
00:28:19,360 --> 00:28:21,080
There are some things
I don't understand and want to ask.

490
00:28:21,160 --> 00:28:24,200
You should be asking your mentor,
not jumping the chain to Sha Sha.

491
00:28:24,800 --> 00:28:27,200
She doesn't have the obligation
or time to mentor you.

492
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:31,200
But Ms. Lin isn't answering my calls

493
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:32,960
or emails or WeChat messages.

494
00:28:33,040 --> 00:28:35,720
Are you tattling
like a grade-schooler now?

495
00:28:36,480 --> 00:28:39,920
<i>Maxmise's policy is that everyone</i>
<i>owns their own work.</i>

496
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:43,120
<i>You took the Bolo Culture project</i>
<i>from Lin Long.</i>

497
00:28:43,200 --> 00:28:46,600
<i>So you are fully responsible</i>
<i>for its success or failure.</i>

498
00:28:46,680 --> 00:28:48,280
The moment you chose to go solo,

499
00:28:48,360 --> 00:28:51,280
you lost the right to complain
that your mentor isn't holding your hand.

500
00:28:51,360 --> 00:28:52,400
Good luck.

501
00:29:07,120 --> 00:29:08,560
XU CHI: MS. LIN, I HAVE AN URGENT ISSUE
WITH BOLO CULTURE

502
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:10,960
Check it now.

503
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:14,120
No need.

504
00:29:14,200 --> 00:29:15,480
We agreed.

505
00:29:15,560 --> 00:29:17,320
Tonight I'm all yours.

506
00:29:18,640 --> 00:29:19,800
I've been taking the meds
to keep the pregnancy safe.

507
00:29:19,880 --> 00:29:21,720
I'm in a much better place now.

508
00:29:21,800 --> 00:29:24,960
I really shouldn't have argued
with you before.

509
00:29:27,040 --> 00:29:29,200
Honey. I'm sorry.

510
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:42,440
I know you've been under a lot of pressure
since I got pregnant.

511
00:29:43,280 --> 00:29:45,920
That day you came to the restaurant,
you were thinking about the baby and me.

512
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:50,200
But I don't know what came over me.

513
00:29:50,800 --> 00:29:53,200
I just can't control my emotions.

514
00:29:53,280 --> 00:29:55,520
-Sometimes I feel like I'm--
-Alright.

515
00:29:55,600 --> 00:29:57,000
Don't blame yourself.

516
00:29:57,520 --> 00:29:58,920
It's normal to have mood swings
during pregnancy.

517
00:29:59,520 --> 00:30:02,680
I just hope you don't
put too much energy into work.

518
00:30:03,200 --> 00:30:04,880
Don't worry. I won't anymore.

519
00:30:04,960 --> 00:30:06,960
I've already talked to the company.

520
00:30:07,480 --> 00:30:08,600
I'm pregnant.

521
00:30:08,680 --> 00:30:10,960
From now on,
I'll avoid overtime as much as I can.

522
00:30:11,040 --> 00:30:13,880
I'll start my maternity leave 30 days
before my due date.

523
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:16,720
And after the baby's born,
I'll make more time for family.

524
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:19,360
I promise to raise him to be
as smart as you.

525
00:30:21,040 --> 00:30:23,720
Honestly, I've never been
against you working.

526
00:30:23,800 --> 00:30:25,160
A second income is a good thing.

527
00:30:25,800 --> 00:30:27,520
But consulting is exhausting.

528
00:30:27,600 --> 00:30:28,720
And you're always working late.

529
00:30:29,240 --> 00:30:31,800
Why not switch to something easier?

530
00:30:34,120 --> 00:30:35,600
What's more important, family or work?

531
00:30:35,680 --> 00:30:37,560
Family, of course.

532
00:30:38,240 --> 00:30:40,480
What matters most is that we build
a good life together.

533
00:30:40,560 --> 00:30:41,520
Right?

534
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:45,640
Come on. Have some fish.

535
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:55,880
<i>This is your first business trip.</i>

536
00:30:55,960 --> 00:30:58,040
<i>So, don't expect</i>
<i>to wow the client right away.</i>

537
00:30:58,120 --> 00:30:59,240
Lower your expectations.

538
00:30:59,320 --> 00:31:03,160
Try to understand their real situation
and what they truly need.

539
00:31:04,680 --> 00:31:08,240
Can you just tell us straight up
what we actually need to do

540
00:31:08,320 --> 00:31:11,760
to get the veteran Qingyi employees
to integrate into our group,

541
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:13,280
fall in line,

542
00:31:13,800 --> 00:31:16,240
and most importantly,
stay motivated at the same time?

543
00:31:17,360 --> 00:31:18,560
We haven't even spoken yet,

544
00:31:18,640 --> 00:31:19,400
-and you're already jumping in?
-All these rules and regulations

545
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:20,240
don't fit our company's growth!

546
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:21,480
-I have two more meetings this afternoon.
-<i>Just because you spoke first…</i>

547
00:31:21,560 --> 00:31:22,880
-I don't have time for financial reports.
-<i>I'm telling you,</i>

548
00:31:22,960 --> 00:31:24,600
<i>either you make it work or forget it!</i>

549
00:31:25,320 --> 00:31:28,120
Your arrangements for regular employees
are not bad,

550
00:31:28,200 --> 00:31:31,880
but what I want
is a more effective overall solution,

551
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:35,120
not some simple compensation reform deck.

552
00:31:41,520 --> 00:31:44,320
MIDDLE AND LOWER MANAGEMENT

553
00:31:46,520 --> 00:31:48,600
What was it that convinced him last time?

554
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:50,600
Since your company isn't short on cash,

555
00:31:50,680 --> 00:31:53,480
and all you care about is Qingyi's IPs,

556
00:31:53,560 --> 00:31:55,080
why not start fresh?

557
00:31:55,160 --> 00:31:56,440
Go on.

558
00:32:03,200 --> 00:32:04,680
SENIOR MANAGEMENT

559
00:32:04,760 --> 00:32:06,640
Keep the senior executives for now.

560
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:13,720
MR. SHEN, BOLO CULTURE

561
00:32:16,080 --> 00:32:17,400
CALL

562
00:32:18,320 --> 00:32:20,880
VIDEO CALL, VOICE CALL

563
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:31,760
YE THE LEGEND

564
00:32:37,560 --> 00:32:39,480
<i>Richard. Can I ask you something?</i>

565
00:32:39,560 --> 00:32:42,080
<i>It's about the project</i>
<i>I'm on during this business trip.</i>

566
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:44,800
<i>Maxmise is helping Bolo Culture</i>
<i>with organizational efficiency.</i>

567
00:32:44,880 --> 00:32:47,080
<i>We had good communication</i>
<i>with their leadership before,</i>

568
00:32:47,160 --> 00:32:51,160
<i>but their boss just blew up</i>
<i>and rejected the whole proposal.</i>

569
00:32:51,240 --> 00:32:52,440
<i>See image.</i>

570
00:32:59,760 --> 00:33:01,000
So, as my interviewer,

571
00:33:01,520 --> 00:33:04,400
teach me how to land
a big deal like Tianhe Air.

572
00:33:05,080 --> 00:33:07,240
Our firms are competitors.

573
00:33:07,320 --> 00:33:08,280
That's confidential.

574
00:33:08,360 --> 00:33:09,200
Can I just tell you that?

575
00:33:09,800 --> 00:33:11,480
Then why did you teach me
how to pick restaurants?

576
00:33:12,080 --> 00:33:13,560
Most people don't need to be taught that.

577
00:33:14,160 --> 00:33:15,080
Wait.

578
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:18,440
If I ask him every time I hit a problem,

579
00:33:19,200 --> 00:33:21,280
isn't that just cheating
with a walkthrough?

580
00:33:24,800 --> 00:33:26,000
RECALL THE MESSAGE

581
00:33:26,600 --> 00:33:27,680
MESSAGE RECALLED

582
00:33:29,720 --> 00:33:32,480
COULD I ASK YOU FOR SOME ADVICE, RICHARD?

583
00:33:38,240 --> 00:33:39,280
Who are you texting?

584
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:42,680
One second you're frowning,
and the next you're smiling.

585
00:33:42,760 --> 00:33:43,840
Got a crush or something?

586
00:33:45,160 --> 00:33:46,000
Just a young lady

587
00:33:46,080 --> 00:33:47,200
in the same industry as us.

588
00:33:47,720 --> 00:33:49,560
She sent me a long WeChat message earlier.

589
00:33:49,640 --> 00:33:51,840
Probably felt something
she said wasn't right,

590
00:33:51,920 --> 00:33:53,840
so she recalled it and went to revise it.

591
00:33:54,560 --> 00:33:56,480
A young lady?

592
00:33:58,440 --> 00:34:00,520
I… I've seen her before.

593
00:34:00,600 --> 00:34:01,560
Right here.

594
00:34:01,640 --> 00:34:03,600
You sat here, and she sat there.
The one I saw.

595
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:06,600
Oh my goodness, Ye.

596
00:34:06,680 --> 00:34:07,720
You're really something.

597
00:34:07,800 --> 00:34:09,920
Such a young girlfriend.

598
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:10,960
Stop it.

599
00:34:11,040 --> 00:34:13,280
I genuinely think she's talented.

600
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:15,360
And her work style

601
00:34:15,440 --> 00:34:19,159
and the problems she runs into
remind me of myself back then.

602
00:34:20,199 --> 00:34:22,199
I took a lot of wrong turns.

603
00:34:22,280 --> 00:34:25,920
I don't want her
to make the same mistakes.

604
00:34:27,199 --> 00:34:30,880
So, when are you starting your plan?

605
00:34:30,960 --> 00:34:33,120
Just say the word
if you need anything from me.

606
00:34:36,360 --> 00:34:38,400
That's actually why
I asked you to come today.

607
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:46,840
FOLIC ACID TABLETS

608
00:34:54,080 --> 00:34:56,400
Sure enough. Got him
a new graphics card and he's happy.

609
00:34:56,480 --> 00:34:58,280
He's downloading games like crazy now.

610
00:34:58,360 --> 00:34:59,920
<i>That's good.</i>

611
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:02,520
Couples shouldn't stay
in a cold war forever.

612
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:04,240
And think about it.

613
00:35:04,320 --> 00:35:05,640
When you're in the delivery room,

614
00:35:05,720 --> 00:35:07,760
if he makes a decision while angry,

615
00:35:07,840 --> 00:35:09,160
you'll be the one suffering for life.

616
00:35:10,040 --> 00:35:11,000
<i>It's fine now.</i>

617
00:35:11,080 --> 00:35:12,560
<i>He's happy, and you're happy.</i>

618
00:35:13,560 --> 00:35:15,240
But I'm not happy at all.

619
00:35:15,320 --> 00:35:17,080
I actually feel kind of sad.

620
00:35:18,320 --> 00:35:20,920
Tactics like playing weak
and pleasing people

621
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:22,400
are what I used to use on clients.

622
00:35:22,480 --> 00:35:23,680
But now?

623
00:35:23,760 --> 00:35:28,040
Now I have to use them
on a man I once loved.

624
00:35:29,200 --> 00:35:30,200
<i>Don't overthink it.</i>

625
00:35:31,680 --> 00:35:32,840
But I'm not giving up.

626
00:35:33,360 --> 00:35:34,360
Once this phase is over,

627
00:35:34,440 --> 00:35:38,120
I'm taking back everything I've given up.

628
00:35:38,200 --> 00:35:40,200
You still want Xu Chi out?

629
00:35:40,720 --> 00:35:42,760
Take it easy.

630
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:46,800
I already gave her low scores
in the newbie challenge camp.

631
00:35:47,560 --> 00:35:49,800
Don't worry. I've let it go.

632
00:35:49,880 --> 00:35:51,680
If she wants to fight, fine by me.

633
00:35:51,760 --> 00:35:54,880
But I'm not giving her
any useful guidance or advice anymore.

634
00:35:54,960 --> 00:35:58,160
At most, I'll reply to her emails
with a "You can try."

635
00:35:59,920 --> 00:36:02,720
<i>Does she really think making slide decks</i>
<i>is all it takes to be a consultant?</i>

636
00:36:02,800 --> 00:36:05,200
This industry runs on experience.

637
00:36:05,280 --> 00:36:08,960
Without a mentor walking you
through real-world projects,

638
00:36:09,040 --> 00:36:10,680
even a genius
is all theory and no practice.

639
00:36:19,520 --> 00:36:20,400
Mr. Shen.

640
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:21,840
What are you doing here?

641
00:36:21,920 --> 00:36:23,600
I was afraid it'd be too late
by the time I got to Beijing.

642
00:36:23,680 --> 00:36:25,480
So now's a good time to talk.

643
00:36:26,280 --> 00:36:28,080
This is the second version
of the proposal I rushed out.

644
00:36:28,160 --> 00:36:29,240
Please take a look.

645
00:36:30,960 --> 00:36:32,840
"Streamline the HR structure."

646
00:36:32,920 --> 00:36:36,440
"Hollow out Qingyi Literature's
existing senior management?"

647
00:36:36,520 --> 00:36:38,080
If I'm not mistaken,

648
00:36:38,160 --> 00:36:41,440
you're looking to address not just
Qingyi's middle and lower management,

649
00:36:41,520 --> 00:36:42,360
but also the senior level.

650
00:36:44,080 --> 00:36:46,680
So your consulting needs have changed.

651
00:36:48,120 --> 00:36:49,160
Have a seat.

652
00:36:52,240 --> 00:36:57,800
You acquired Qingyi Literature
just for their IPs, right?

653
00:36:57,880 --> 00:37:00,040
But because Qingyi has too many employees,

654
00:37:00,120 --> 00:37:04,160
you're worried they'll affect
Bolo's corporate culture.

655
00:37:04,240 --> 00:37:06,880
That's why you brought in Maxmise.

656
00:37:06,960 --> 00:37:09,160
You want them to integrate
without causing you any trouble.

657
00:37:10,040 --> 00:37:13,080
My initial plan to lay off all
of Qingyi's middle and lower management

658
00:37:13,160 --> 00:37:14,200
appealed to you

659
00:37:14,280 --> 00:37:17,040
because it offered
a clean, quick solution.

660
00:37:17,720 --> 00:37:18,680
Keep the senior executives for now.

661
00:37:18,760 --> 00:37:20,360
Let all other former
Qingyi employees leave

662
00:37:20,440 --> 00:37:21,960
with the market's best severance package

663
00:37:22,040 --> 00:37:23,640
of 2N plus 10.

664
00:37:23,720 --> 00:37:25,400
But gradually, you realized

665
00:37:25,480 --> 00:37:28,000
that Qingyi's senior management
is also a liability.

666
00:37:28,080 --> 00:37:28,960
You want to deal with them too.

667
00:37:29,040 --> 00:37:31,160
-You're already jumping in?
-All these rules and regulations…

668
00:37:31,240 --> 00:37:32,480
-I am telling you…
-Nonsense!

669
00:37:33,280 --> 00:37:35,720
Either you make it work or forget it!

670
00:37:36,600 --> 00:37:38,080
But on a conscious level,

671
00:37:38,160 --> 00:37:41,360
you might not have been able
to articulate what you actually needed.

672
00:37:41,440 --> 00:37:44,960
That's why you blew up
at me this afternoon.

673
00:37:45,040 --> 00:37:46,920
I'm paying you consultants big money

674
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:49,680
to help Qingyi Literature
integrate into us smoothly.

675
00:37:49,760 --> 00:37:52,040
Not some simple compensation reform deck.

676
00:37:54,720 --> 00:37:56,880
Looks like you know me better
than I know myself.

677
00:37:58,120 --> 00:38:00,520
In the future, you could not only
do management consulting,

678
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:01,760
but also moonlight as a shrink.

679
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:06,920
Either way, consulting is essentially
a personal service.

680
00:38:07,680 --> 00:38:09,520
We use our own experience to help clients

681
00:38:09,600 --> 00:38:11,560
analyze problems
from an outside perspective.

682
00:38:11,640 --> 00:38:15,240
To help you see the elephant
in the room you couldn't see before.

683
00:38:15,840 --> 00:38:16,720
But regardless,

684
00:38:16,800 --> 00:38:19,880
I owe you an apology
for that outburst this afternoon.

685
00:38:20,760 --> 00:38:21,720
But as the client,

686
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:23,080
I'm allowed to be a little temperamental.

687
00:38:23,160 --> 00:38:24,800
-You can forgive that, right?
-Of course.

688
00:38:25,320 --> 00:38:28,920
Set up an overseas
business unit headquartered in Singapore.

689
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:31,360
Transfer all of Qingyi's
senior management there.

690
00:38:32,440 --> 00:38:34,640
If they can't integrate
into Bolo's culture,

691
00:38:34,720 --> 00:38:36,160
just ship them all overseas.

692
00:38:36,240 --> 00:38:38,800
First, Bolo is expanding
its overseas business.

693
00:38:38,880 --> 00:38:42,960
Second, most of Qingyi's senior managers
have kids in primary or middle school.

694
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:47,040
If you offer a good title, solid pay,
and great benefits,

695
00:38:47,120 --> 00:38:49,480
their families will push them to go.

696
00:38:49,560 --> 00:38:51,200
It's an overseas degree, after all.

697
00:38:51,720 --> 00:38:54,760
Third, if they actually
make something of themselves over there,

698
00:38:54,840 --> 00:38:56,960
it's a win for Bolo too.

699
00:38:58,640 --> 00:39:00,480
-Interesting.
-Of course,

700
00:39:00,560 --> 00:39:02,560
the formal proposal
won't be written exactly like this.

701
00:39:02,640 --> 00:39:05,320
You just need to understand the real
purpose of this consulting engagement.

702
00:39:06,360 --> 00:39:07,200
Mr. Shen, I promise

703
00:39:07,280 --> 00:39:10,160
Maxmise will put together
a top-notch consulting team.

704
00:39:10,240 --> 00:39:11,320
We'll craft a solution
that covers everything,

705
00:39:11,400 --> 00:39:13,200
from potential restructuring
and vision-driven strategy

706
00:39:13,280 --> 00:39:15,360
to scaling your ecosystem
and business model overseas.

707
00:39:15,440 --> 00:39:17,320
We'll make sure most
of Bolo and Qingyi's employees

708
00:39:17,400 --> 00:39:18,920
are on board and happy with the outcome.

709
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:22,200
That way, your consulting fees
are money well spent.

710
00:39:23,720 --> 00:39:25,920
I like your big words this time.

711
00:39:28,440 --> 00:39:29,680
Tell me more.
